# .env.local.example, the settings kriegerdataforge-portfolio needs that work only on this machine (env standard, cicd ADR D-030)
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local holds values that work only on this machine, local
# passwords, keys, ports and URLs, and any AI session may read it, so it never holds a credential. A credential,
# anything that works beyond this machine, goes in .env.kdf, see .env.kdf.example.
#
# kriegerdataforge-portfolio needs no local only setting today. The three NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_* keys and
# GH_PACKAGES_PAT moved to .env.kdf. The file still has to exist, since compose reads it with --env-file, and
# make setup creates it from this example.
